"# New Captain Marvel trailer\nAnd we see what I’m pretty sure are SWORD scientists, based on their black and white color scheme\n![](dayone-moment://11706DDA797144F39A81874A6FDB39E2)\nI’m specifically looking at this guy\n![](dayone-moment://4A3BE07B215840BF8EC0BAF5D8DB1892)\nWe’re getting closer and closer\nAnd\nAAAAANNNNNNDDDDDDD\nAn extra thing I’m realizing is that a black and white jumpsuit - specifically, black with white details - is... just what the FF look like sometimes. Not even in Future Foundation, but also just kinda what the Byrne negative outfits are.\n\nSo what do you get when you combine a SWORD(/SABER) scientist jumpsuit...\nWith the design work on Monica’s SWORD shirt in *Wandavision*...\n![](dayone-moment://70A5C679A01A474BBF37B1234F09CB72)\nAnd invert the colors? \n\nPerhaps in a John Byrne-inspired movie?\n\n(Also look how the design of the jumpsuit is almost noting except, floating in white space, that V shape that every costume has)\n* * *\n\nMeanwhile, some X-Men ’97 footage was shown at comic con (which I guess is happening now)\n> During the ‘Designing the X-Men’ panel at San Diego Comic-Con 2023, Marvel surprised attendees with new footage from X-Men '97.\n> \n> \n> \n> One of the clips shows the X-Men team interrogating the villainous Dr. Trask, with Jean Grey lending a hand to enter his mind during the process. Cyclops even gets his moment to say his iconic \"To me, my X-Men\" line.\n> \n> \n> \n> Another clip featured Cyclops slowing down several X-Men members with his laser beams as they were falling out of the air.\n> \n> \n> \n> Additionally, it was confirmed that Jean Grey will be pregnant, and both Archangel and Bishop will be official members of the team.\n> \n> \n> \n> Marvel also gave an official update on the X-Men '97 animated series' future, revealing that Season 2 is still in development and “nearing completion”\n\n\n> \\#SDCC showed an exclusive look at a clip of ‘X-MEN ‘97’ which revealed Master Mold, a pregnant Jean Grey, Archangel and Bishop as official members of the team, and Cyclops saying the classic “To me my X-Men” line.\n\n* * *\n\nI want to work out wording for what I have to say about the costumes on the weekly talk thread before it’s posted\n\n...\n\nWhat do you get when you cross the SWORD/SABER scientist jumpsuit on the left at [1:34 in the Marvels trailer](<https://youtu.be/wS_qbDztgVY?t=94>) with the design work on (Monica’s SWORD outfit in Wandavision)[[https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/monica-episode-7-1613765354.png](<https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/monica-episode-7-1613765354.png>)]?\n\nPersonally, I think you get a Fantastic Four jumpsuit. More specifically, you get something that resembles John Byrne’s original baggy jumpsuit approach to the FF’s costumes mixed with his later nearly-black-and-white costume color scheme.\n\nI think we’ve heard in the past that Feige is a fan of Byrne, and I think the supposed inclusion of Galactus and Terrax in the upcoming Fantastic Four movie might suggest a Byrne-inspired story. I also think that, since comic book Reed started his career in the space program, it makes sense that movie Reed would be associated with SWORD.\n\nAll this to say, I think they’ve been dropping Fantastic Four costume hints since *Wandavision*.\n* * *\n\nHmm\nThe “marvel studios rumors” one came up, but not the “spoilers” one yet\n8:30, maybe?\nLet’s check!\nOh, the last one was at 10:45am\nOkay I should work then\n\n* * *\nUpdate\n\\~+5 on the \"rumors\" thread\n\\-1 on the \"spoilers\" thread (huh.)\nAnd I forgot to add \"then invert the colors\" to the first paragraph!\nSo now I've edited that.\n"